	"AuthorLabel": "norisu",
	"Description": "loosely inspired by the [url=http://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/1244/?]vintage interface mod[/url] by [url=http://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/users/34767255/?]manakirel[/url], this mod changes the ui into one of five pastel colors: mint, soda, lavender, \r<br />sunflower, and tangerine&#33; almost all of the ui is changed, save for some\r<br /> of the fonts&#33; if you have suggestions on improving the colors/colors you&#39;d like to see, let me know&#33;\r<br />\r<br />update: thanks again to [url=http://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/users/34767255/?]manakirel[/url] for letting me know how to fix the window lighting issue, everything should be fine now&#33;&#33;\r<br />\r<br />update 2: added a new soft beige/chocolate color&#33;&#33;\r<br />\r<br />notes on installation: the files &#39;cursors,&#39; &#39;dialogboxgreen,&#39; &#39;font_bold,&#39; &#39;junimonote,&#39; &#39;letterbg,&#39; and &#39;textbox&#39; go in the loosesprites folder, the files &#39;smallfont,&#39; &#39;spritefont1,&#39; &#39;tinyfont,&#39; and &#39;tinyfontborder&#39; go in the fonts folder, the file &#39;menutiles&#39; goes in the maps folder, and the file &#39;titlebuttons&#39; goes in the minigames folder",
